  /* Pressed, a glass button lights up white, as iOS 26's interactive Liquid Glass does (the app's
     .glassEffect(.regular.interactive())): at once on the press, easing back on release. A click from the keyboard
     shows it briefly too (the "pressed" class). The scale is its own property, so the transforms above stay as
     they are. */
  .yo-phone .screen .fab, .yo-phone .screen .zoom {
    transition: opacity 0.25s ease, transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1), scale 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1),
